  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Digital Workforce Development (formerly USAID Digital Future Cambodia )</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cambodia):  .The USAID Digital Future Cambodia activity aims to create a cohort of Cambodian youth with enterprise-driven skills, training, and qualifications that will help them contribute to Cambodian society and succeed in a modern digital economy. The activity will also support an open internet and freedom of information exchange in order to encourage competition, innovation, and promote international standards for information technology (IT) certification and advance Cambodia&apos;s economic diversification in the digital age. FY 2021 funds will be used to strengthen targeted IT certifications, short-courses, non-degree programs, and bachelor&apos;s degrees offered by Cambodian higher education institutions (HEIs), build capacity of HEI faculty to prepare them to meet accreditation standards, and increase scholarship, internship, and networking opportunities to support practical skill-building and linkages to job opportunities for Cambodian youth...The activity supports all USAID/Cambodia&apos;s CDCS 2020-2025 Development Objectives by promoting internet freedom of information exchange, empowering youth through education and enterprise-driven job skills, and supporting sustainable economic livelihoods through market-based solutions. The activity will contribute to U.S. foreign policy priorities in the Indo-Pacific region by building partnerships between U.S. and Cambodian universities and expanding digital access, thus reducing malign regional influence and supporting growing economic opportunities and prosperity for Cambodians and Americans. The activity will also support multiple priorities of the Administration, including 1) Renewing and championing democracy and human rights; 2) Building a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workforce; and 3) Modernizing IT, data, and mobility. The activity will be competitively awarded based on the best value to the U.S. government, in accordance with federal procurement regulations..</narrative>
  </description>
